Background blur that holds still: changes to @livekit/track-processors 0.8.1,
applied to its TypeScript source by scripts/vendor-blur.mjs before bundling.
Stock, the blurred background ripples: it is shrunk to a quarter by taking one
pixel in sixteen, so a patterned wall aliases and shimmers with every bit of
camera noise; the Gaussian is cut off at one sigma, which makes it a box blur
with a lattice of its own; and the person's mask is new every frame.

- downSampler.ts: the quarter-size copy averages each 4x4 block (four
  bilinear taps), so nothing aliases.
- blurShader.ts: sigma is a third of the radius, so the kernel reaches three
  sigmas; up to 32 taps a side.
- index.ts: the radius is given for a frame whose short side is 720 pixels and
  scaled to the frame; the mask is blended with the previous one, keeping
  exp(-elapsed / 50 ms) of it (maskSmoothShader.ts).
- every shader: highp. On phones mediump is a 16-bit float, too coarse to
  address a 720-pixel texture, so samples snap and the picture wobbles.

And one fix (2026-10-04), in BackgroundTransformer.ts: blur switched off
while its first frame waits to paint no longer freezes the page. transform
checks isDisabled once, then the first frame awaits requestVideoFrameCallback;
destroy closed the segmenter meanwhile, and the frame went on into it. The
wasm never returned. Now transform checks again after the wait, destroy takes
the segmenter off before closing it, and segmentation without one resolves at
once.

